# FAQ — NextChapter Schedule Builder

Questions marked **[YOU FILL IN]** need your program's specifics — everyone
else is answered by how the app actually works.

## For students

**I lost my code — can you find my schedule?**
Technically: no, not through the app itself. By design, nothing in this app is
tied to your name, but staff can get you a copy of your schedule.

**Does this cost anything / do I need a Google account?**
No Google account is needed to build or print a schedule. A Google
account **is** needed only if you want to open the "Create my Google
Doc/Sheet" links (same as needing an account to open any Google file).

**What if none of the activities match what I picked?**
The app will tell you no match was found and suggest asking a staff
member.

**Can staff help me fill this out?**
Yes, please make an appointment in advance!

**What devices/browsers does this work on?**
Any modern phone, tablet, or computer browser (Chrome, Safari, Edge,
Firefox). No app download needed.

## For staff

**Will a new Google Sheet get created every month?**
Two different things to know:
- The **shared class list** (the Sheet you deployed Apps Script from) is
  one permanent Sheet — updating it each month **overwrites** the
  previous list. [YOU FILL IN: your chosen archive habit, e.g. "duplicate
  the Classes tab and rename it to the month before saving"]
- Each **student's individual exported Sheet/Doc** is a brand-new file,
  created fresh every time they click "Create my Google Sheet/Doc." These
  accumulate over time and are not automatically cleaned up.

**Can two staff members update the class list at the same time?**
Not safely — the last person to click "Save for all students" overwrites
whatever the sheet currently has. [YOU FILL IN: your team's coordination
plan, e.g. "only front desk updates the list, once a month."]

**Who owns the Google Drive files this creates?**
Whichever Google account deployed the Apps Script and owns the backend
Sheet. [YOU FILL IN: confirm this is your program's account, not a
personal one, before handoff — or document the transfer plan.]

**How do we change the staff password?**
Apps Script editor → Project Settings → Script Properties →
`STAFF_PASSWORD`. Takes effect immediately, no redeploy needed. [YOU FILL
IN: how often you'll rotate it / who has authority to change it.]

**What if the newsletter paste-parser gets something wrong?**
Expected — it's a shortcut, not a guarantee. Always review the table
after parsing before saving. [YOU FILL IN: who's responsible for that
review each month.]

**What happens to last month's exported student Sheets/Docs?**
Nothing automatic — they stay in Drive indefinitely with editable links.
[YOU FILL IN: your cleanup cadence, e.g. quarterly review and deletion of
old files.]

## Technical / accessibility

**Is this HIPAA compliant?**
By design, the app never collects a name or identifying information, so
there's no PHI in this system to protect — that's what keeps it out of
HIPAA's technical requirements. See the HIPAA section in `README.md` for
the full explanation, and the line where that stops being true (a
counselor needing to see which specific student gave which answers).

**Is this accessible (WCAG 2.2)?**
Built with that as a first-class goal — see the Accessibility section of
`README.md` for specifics. [YOU FILL IN: results of your own accessibility
audit once you've run it, plus any fixes made as a result.]

